window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/resources/security-v27-024-38c41bdf6c77b07f.json"]={sha256:"38c41bdf6c77b07f1ad5f6970c3a40f57bc8ab702a02edc3e71cccc4932cac79",value:{"sources":[{"id":"v27-case-ffaa4c5ed4171d66","url":"https://openfga.dev/docs/modeling/parent-child","title":"OpenFGA parent-child authorization modeling","titleEn":"OpenFGA parent-child authorization modeling","publisher":"OpenFGA","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."},{"id":"v27-case-f0e4f6b787ddb81f","url":"https://openfga.dev/docs/modeling/blocklists","title":"OpenFGA blocklists","titleEn":"OpenFGA blocklists","publisher":"OpenFGA","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"media":{"courses":[{"courseId":"security-v27-024","videos":[],"guides":[]}]},"related":{"courses":[{"courseId":"security-v27-024","related":[{"id":"security-v27-025","referenceUrls":["https://docs.cedarpolicy.com/auth/authorization.html"],"title":"Cedar：forbid優先與錯誤政策的診斷契約","titleEn":"Cedar: forbid precedence and erroneous-policy diagnostics","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：60%與50%由集合運算取得，雙路徑不重複計數，封鎖及跨租戶負例都不得通過。 交付fga-tuples.json、逐人證明路徑及集合差異表；所有人名與文件ID都為本地假資料。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Obtain 60 and 50 percent from set operations, avoid duplicate path counting and reject blocked-user and cross-tenant counterexamples. Deliver fga-tuples.json, per-user proof paths and set-difference tables. All user and document identifiers are local fixtures, and the exercise writes no tuples to a hosted service.","difference":"建立12筆PARC請求與permit、forbid、缺屬性政策；保存引擎決策、determining policies及errors，再實作本地敏感操作有錯誤即暫緩的外層規則。","differenceEn":"Build 12 PARC requests and permit, forbid and missing-attribute policies. Preserve the engine decision, determining policies and errors, then add a clearly separate application rule that withholds sensitive operations when diagnostics contain errors.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["本地模型將直接與繼承讀者取聯集，再扣除封鎖集合；同一使用者有兩條路徑仍只計一次。規則必須以選定模型ID固定，避免測試途中換模型。 讀者聯集共8人，其中2人被封鎖；總使用者10人，另2人沒有任何讀取路徑。 有效讀者(8−2)/10×100=60%；另封鎖一名原本有效讀者後為(8−3)/10×100=50%。","引擎略過錯誤政策不代表應用必須忽略錯誤；本課外層准入要求Allow且errors為空，將引擎語意與產品選定規則分開測試。 12筆中引擎有8筆Allow，其中2筆伴隨錯誤診斷；其他4筆Deny，固定母體並保留各政策ID。 外層准入率(8−2)/12×100=50%；修復其中一筆錯誤且引擎仍Allow後為(8−1)/12×100≈58.333%。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["The local model unions direct and inherited readers, then subtracts blocked users. Count a user once even when two paths grant access. Pin the authorization model ID so a changed model cannot silently alter the interpretation during evaluation. The reader union contains eight users, two of whom are blocked. Ten users form the fixed population; the other two have no read path. Explicitly list overlaps between direct and inherited grants to avoid double counting. Effective readership is (8−2)/10×100=60 percent. Blocking one additional previously eligible reader gives (8−3)/10×100=50 percent, while the inherited and direct grant sets remain unchanged.","Skipping an erroneous policy inside the engine does not require the application to ignore diagnostics. The local wrapper admits only Allow with an empty error list, testing engine semantics separately from the product decision layered above them. Of 12 requests the engine allows eight, including two with error diagnostics. Four are denied. Keep the population and policy IDs fixed so that wrapper withholding cannot be mistaken for a change in Cedar engine behavior. Wrapper admission is (8−2)/12×100=50 percent. Repairing one error while retaining its engine Allow gives (8−1)/12×100, approximately 58.333 percent; the other error still withholds the operation.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]},{"id":"security-v27-034","referenceUrls":["https://github.com/sigstore/architecture-docs/blob/main/rekor-spec.md"],"title":"Rekor：檢查點連續性與分裂視圖證據限制","titleEn":"Rekor: checkpoint continuity and limits of split-view evidence","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：60%與50%由集合運算取得，雙路徑不重複計數，封鎖及跨租戶負例都不得通過。 交付fga-tuples.json、逐人證明路徑及集合差異表；所有人名與文件ID都為本地假資料。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Obtain 60 and 50 percent from set operations, avoid duplicate path counting and reject blocked-user and cross-tenant counterexamples. Deliver fga-tuples.json, per-user proof paths and set-difference tables. All user and document identifiers are local fixtures, and the exercise writes no tuples to a hosted service.","difference":"建立可信起始檢查點、後續樹大小、根雜湊與證明狀態；每個檢查點先驗證簽章，再依所屬log/shard比較連續性。","differenceEn":"Build a trusted initial checkpoint and later tree sizes, root hashes and proof results. Verify checkpoint signatures before continuity checks, keeping log and shard identifiers explicit so unrelated trees cannot be compared as one append-only sequence.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["本地模型將直接與繼承讀者取聯集，再扣除封鎖集合；同一使用者有兩條路徑仍只計一次。規則必須以選定模型ID固定，避免測試途中換模型。 讀者聯集共8人，其中2人被封鎖；總使用者10人，另2人沒有任何讀取路徑。 有效讀者(8−2)/10×100=60%；另封鎖一名原本有效讀者後為(8−3)/10×100=50%。","本課計算已驗證連續轉移佔所有預期轉移的比例；這是證據覆蓋指標，不是透明日誌誠實機率。簽章正確並不單獨證明兩個根前綴一致。 有7個依序檢查點形成6段轉移，其中4段具有效一致性證明，2段缺證明；所有簽章與log識別已先通過。 覆蓋率4/(7−1)×100≈66.667%；補齊一段有效證明後為5/6×100≈83.333%，仍有一段未確認。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["The local model unions direct and inherited readers, then subtracts blocked users. Count a user once even when two paths grant access. Pin the authorization model ID so a changed model cannot silently alter the interpretation during evaluation. The reader union contains eight users, two of whom are blocked. Ten users form the fixed population; the other two have no read path. Explicitly list overlaps between direct and inherited grants to avoid double counting. Effective readership is (8−2)/10×100=60 percent. Blocking one additional previously eligible reader gives (8−3)/10×100=50 percent, while the inherited and direct grant sets remain unchanged.","Measure verified consecutive transitions among expected transitions as evidence coverage, not the probability that a log is honest. Valid checkpoint signatures alone do not establish that one committed tree is an append-only prefix of another. Seven ordered checkpoints create six transitions. Four have valid consistency proofs and two lack them; signatures and log identities have already passed independent checks, isolating continuity evidence from checkpoint authentication. Coverage is 4/(7−1)×100, approximately 66.667 percent. Adding one valid proof yields 5/6×100, approximately 83.333 percent, leaving a transition unresolved rather than proving complete continuity.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]}],"references":[{"id":"v27-case-1442718f9f4fd115","url":"https://docs.cedarpolicy.com/auth/authorization.html","title":"How Cedar authorization works","titleEn":"How Cedar authorization works","publisher":"Cedar","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."},{"id":"v27-case-3992c3cc9abcfa82","url":"https://github.com/sigstore/architecture-docs/blob/main/rekor-spec.md","title":"Rekor transparency service specification","titleEn":"Rekor transparency service specification","publisher":"Sigstore","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"overview":"比較相鄰案例與另一組案例的模型、可量測結果及可轉移的驗證方法。","overviewEn":"Compare neighboring and cross-group cases by model, measurable outcome, and transferable verification method."}]},"places":{"courses":[]},"vendors":{"courses":[],"vendors":[]}}};
